# One line ending in the repository, because this now gets cloned onto Windows
# and macOS by people who will diff each other's changes. Without this, git's
# core.autocrlf default rewrites on checkout per-machine and the first
# cross-platform edit shows every line as changed.
#
# LF in the repo and in the working tree: this is a Node project run as
# `node deident.mjs`, and nothing here is opened by a Windows tool that needs
# CRLF. Session logs are JSONL, which is LF by definition.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixture corpora and archives are compared byte for byte. Never touch them.
*.zip binary
*.jsonl -text
